  "summary_en": "Japanese AMED guidebook for developers of robotic care devices, structured along a V-model development process: concept sheet, human-centred design, risk assessment templates (ISO 12100/JIS B 9700), safety requirements mapped to ISO 13482, safety testing, field trials with ethics review, standardisation status, and deployment guidelines.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Robotic care devices should be developed as tools for 'improving care', assessing positive and negative impacts on care receivers using ICF.",
   "Development follows a V-model with a development concept sheet covering indications, contraindications and foreseeable negatives.",
   "Risk assessment templates use a three-step method (inherent safe design, safeguarding, information for use) with risk score R=S×(F+Ps+A).",
   "Safety requirements per device type are mapped to ISO 13482 hazard list and JIS/ISO standards.",
   "Field trials require safety verification and ethics review application; developers and users should agree on liability sharing, insurance and training."
  ],
